<<^ code=`&#x0002;`>>

```toml meta
cacheable = true
l-space   = "stable"
role      = "mint or load a persona root at a handle index, with its private label"
tags      = ["lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance", "lar:///face.persona.mints", "candidate"]
title     = "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/face.persona.mints"
type      = "text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki"
uri-path  = "ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/face.persona.mints"
```

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! face.persona.mints ~ a persona root at one handle index

`lares persona new <index> name='<petname>'` mints a persona root at that handle index, or loads the one standing there, and keeps its private label. `--handle '<Handle>'` declares its outward name apart from the label; `--seat [--chair <label>]` stands it for a Kahu chair on this node, with a private chair label and no Handle needed; `--split-root` opts into the 2-of-3 recovery split. The index reads within the derivation's range and this vessel's slot ceiling (`LAR_PERSONA_SLOTS`); a herm mints no root, and a place with no face yet founds one first.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ new · seat · handle

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`new` params=`index/1 name/garden ~ mint a persona root at h1`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`seat` params=`index/1 name/garden seat/true chair/first-chair ~ stand it for a Kahu chair`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`handle` params=`index/1 name/garden handle/Gardener split-root/true ~ declare a Handle and split the root`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ index · name · handle · seat · chair · split-root

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`index` params=`takes/handle-index needs/required seat/1 as/<index> ~ the face's handle index, a whole number from 0`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`name` params=`takes/label needs/required ~ the private pet name`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`handle` params=`takes/name ~ the outward Handle`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`seat` params=`~ stand the face for a Kahu chair on this node`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`chair` params=`takes/label ~ beside --seat, the private chair label`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`split-root` params=`~ opt into the 2-of-3 recovery split`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ hand

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`hand` params=`who/hand key/face-root ~ mints a root sealed on this vessel; a person runs it at their own terminal`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ usage · vessel-composing · vessel-silent · vessel-locked · error

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`usage` params=`cure/[[face.persona.mints index/1 name/garden]] ~ no index, an index out of range or past the slot ceiling, no --name, --chair without --seat, a herm, or no face founded yet`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`vessel-composing` params=`~ an unlock still recomposes the vessel; run again once lares vault status reads ready`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`vessel-silent` params=`~ something holds the store and answers nothing; lares vessel read names the holder`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`vessel-locked` params=`~ the vessel key stands shut; lares vault unlock opens it`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`error` params=`~ the store refused; the message names why`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ minted

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`minted` params=`exit/0 ~ the face's index, label, key and any Handle or seat claim`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins`>>

!! skins ~ cli

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins/cli`>>

!!! lares persona new

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`skin` name=`cli` params=`handler/host spells/[[lares persona new]] ~ the terminal`>>
```

